I've completed the analysis and written the structured output. Here's my run of the 8-step process:

## STEP 1 — DELTA
**NO_DELTA** — Fresh passive re-probes confirm surface identical: `affiliates /rest/public/config` 200, `/rest/user/password/reset` 405, `cable /cable/user-event` 405, all unchanged.

## STEP 2 — PRIORITIZE
- `[PRIO] affiliates.betpanda.io/rest/*, 9.05` — flagship (a9/b9/t9/g8/c7/f8)
- `[PRIO] casino+partners /rest/user/*, 8.15` — BOLA money-flow
- `[PRIO] cable /cable/user-event, 6.90`

## STEP 3-4 — HYPOTHESES (survivors)
1. **[MISCONFIG, 90]** Affiliates wildcard CORS+credentials ATO — re-confirmed this cycle: `access-control-allow-origin: https://evil.com` + `access-control-allow-credentials: true` on the **unauthenticated** public layer, proving it's backend-wide and **unmitigated**. HUMAN-only POC.
2. **[IDOR, 72]** BOLA across shared tenant backend (casino + partners, multi-tenant verified).
3. **[BUSLOGIC, 72]** Unauth cable event injection (PASSIVE/exhausted).

## STEP 5 — NEXT ACTION
`[NEXT] HUMAN`: Obtain an authenticated affiliates session + capture Set-Cookie (SameSite) flags, then run credentialed cross-origin GET `/rest/user/metrics/affiliate` and POST `/rest/user/players` from `Origin: evil.com` — the only blocker to closing the flagship POC.

## STEP 6-7 — LEARNING / RISK
[LEARN] reaffirmed wildcard-credential CORS is backend-wide and unpatched. `[RISK] betpanda: 50` — real and unmitigated finding, but every critical demonstration stays gated on a provisioned test account, and the surface has been static ~5 days.
