Based on my review of all lead files and probe results, here is the 7-Question Gate triage for each surviving hypothesis:

---

## LEAD 1: Wildcard CORS + Credentials on Affiliates REST API
**Asset:** `affiliates.betpanda.io/rest/*`
**Class:** MISCONFIG

| Gate | Answer |
|------|--------|
| Q1 Scope | YES — affiliates.betpanda.io is in-scope (all company-owned infrastructure) |
| Q2 Reachable | YES — public, unauthenticated OPTIONS confirms ACAO reflect + ACAC:true |
| Q3 Impact | YES — cross-origin read of player PII, transactions, password/payout config; cross-origin write to change-password, set-profile, set-deposit-withdraw-limit |
| Q4 Provable | YES — `curl -sS -D- -H "Origin: https://evil.com" https://affiliates.betpanda.io/rest/user` shows ACAO + ACAC:true; authenticated exfil needs 2 affiliate accounts (AUTH_HELPED) |
| Q5 Novel | YES — no prior report found; wildcard CORS + credentials on gambling affiliate platform is uncommon |
| Q6 Not always-rejected | YES — not on the always-rejected list (this is a real misconfiguration, not "OPTIONS enabled") |
| Q7 Reasonable triager | YES — CORS reflecting any origin + credentials on authenticated money-flow API is a textbook critical finding |

**VERDICT: VALID**
**Proof steps:** (1) `curl -sS -D- https://affiliates.betpanda.io/rest/user -H "Origin: https://evil.com"` — confirm ACAO reflected + ACAC:true. (2) Login, capture cookies, then `curl -sS -D- -b cookies.txt https://affiliates.betpanda.io/rest/user/players -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Origin: https://evil.com" -d '{"limit":1,"offset":0}'` — confirm data exfil with CORS headers. (3) Test /rest/user/change-password, /rest/user/set-profile, /rest/agent/set-deposit-withdraw-limit for cross-origin write.
**Impact:** Critical — cross-tenant player PII + financial data exfil + account takeover via password/payout modification on gambling affiliate platform
**CVSS 3.1:** 9.1 (AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:N)
**Reporting channel:** bugs.olivermaicher.eu (private program via Oliver Maicher)

---

## LEAD 2: BOLA/IDOR on Player Wallet & Balance Endpoints
**Asset:** `betpandacasino.io/rest/user/*`
**Class:** IDOR

| Gate | Answer |
|------|--------|
| Q1 Scope | YES — betpandacasino.io is in-scope (betting platform) |
| Q2 Reachable | PARTIAL — auth required (401/403), CORS properly pinned to own origin |
| Q3 Impact | YES — cross-tenant wallet/balance/bonus disclosure or tampering on real-money gambling |
| Q4 Provable | NO — requires 2 user accounts + JWT manipulation (AUTH_HELPED); CORS properly pinned prevents browser-based cross-origin attack; server-side BOLA unconfirmed |
| Q5 Novel | Likely — no evidence of prior report |
| Q6 Not always-rejected | YES |
| Q7 Reasonable triager | PARTIAL — endpoints exist (POST-only balances, 401 settings) but no proof of missing server-side ACL; CORS properly configured reduces attack surface significantly |

**VERDICT: HOLD**
**Reason:** High-potential hypothesis but no passive proof of missing server-side authorization. Needs 2 test accounts + JWT sub-claim manipulation to confirm. CORS properly pinned to own origin (not vulnerable to browser-based attack). Report only if BOLA confirmed with cross-tenant access demo.

---

## LEAD 3: Unauthenticated Event Injection via cable.betpanda.io
**Asset:** `cable.betpanda.io/cable/user-event`
**Class:** BUSLOGIC

| Gate | Answer |
|------|--------|
| Q1 Scope | YES — cable.betpanda.io is in-scope |
| Q2 Reachable | YES — public, no auth, CORS * |
| Q3 Impact | UNCERTAIN — data is "processed and saved" but no evidence it's rendered to other users or triggers XSS; impact depends on server-side processing |
| Q4 Provable | PARTIAL — can send arbitrary JSON and get 200, but cannot observe stored-XSS or injection effect without access to admin dashboards |
| Q5 Novel | YES |
| Q6 Not always-rejected | YES — this is not "OPTIONS enabled" but actual unauthenticated data ingestion |
| Q7 Reasonable triager | PARTIAL — ingestion confirmed but no demonstrated downstream impact (stored XSS, SQL/NoSQL injection, log poisoning). Without proving the payload reaches a dangerous sink, triager may reject as "no impact shown" |

**VERDICT: HOLD**
**Reason:** Unauthenticated ingestion with CORS * is real, but no proof of stored-XSS or injection in downstream systems. Needs admin dashboard access or evidence of data rendering to confirm impact. Recommend probing with XSS payloads + observing if data appears in any reporting interface.

---

## REJECTED LEADS (already eliminated by hunt bot):

| Lead | Verdict | Reason |
|------|---------|--------|
| OAuth redirect_uri bypass (betpanda.io) | INVALID | SPA catch-all — /api/auth/authorize redirects 301 to betpandacasino.io which returns SPA HTML. No server-side OAuth endpoint exists. |
| S3 bucket listing (nano-public.s3) | INVALID | Returns 403 Forbidden — bucket listing disabled |
| k8s dashboard exposure (dashboard.betpanda.io) | INVALID | All probes timeout — ALB likely internal/auth-gated |
| Flipt feature-flag abuse (flags.betpanda.io) | INVALID | Cloudflare JS challenge blocks all passive probes |
| Strapi CMS baseURL override | INVALID | Requires prior XSS to set localStorage; standalone impact is content injection only |
| S3 SSRF via PWA manifest | INVALID | Bucket listing disabled, manifest is static, no query param manipulation |

---

## SUMMARY

| # | Lead | Verdict | CVSS | Report? |
|---|------|---------|------|---------|
| 1 | Affiliates CORS+credentials | **VALID** | 9.1 | YES — bugs.olivermaicher.eu |
| 2 | betpandacasino BOLA/IDOR | **HOLD** | — | Needs 2-account proof first |
| 3 | cable event injection | **HOLD** | — | Needs downstream impact proof |
